========================================================================================================================//====================//==================
⚠️ Current Limitations
====================================================================================================================//========================//==================
- The alarm monitor must be started manually.
- Alarm monitoring does not run automatically in the background.
- Stopwatch lap recording depends on user input.
- Alarm and study records are stored temporarily in memory.
- Data is reset when the notebook kernel restarts.
- The application currently uses a menu-driven interface rather than a graphical interface.

=============================================================//===============================================================================//==================
🚀 Future Enhancements
=============================================================//==============================================================================//===================
The project can be improved further by introducing:

- Graphical User Interface (GUI).
- Permanent data storage using a database.
- Sound notifications for alarms.
- Multiple time zone support.
- Graphical productivity reports.
- Daily and weekly study analytics.
- Customizable themes and clock formats.

=============================================================//===============================================================================//==================
🎯 Project Objective
=============================================================//==============================================================================//===================
The main objective of CLOCK MASTER is to develop a simple and useful Python application that combines everyday time management tools with study productivity tracking.

The project also provides practical experience in Python programming, logical problem-solving, function-based programming, and application development.

